From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Export module symbols for dlopened audio plugins

The synthesis modules open the audio output plugins (spd_pipewire,
spd_pulse, spd_alsa) at runtime with dlopen(RTLD_NOW); the plugins
resolve symbols such as MSG() from the module executable, so the module
must export its dynamic symbols. Upstream relies on GNU libtool turning
`-dlopen force` on a program into `-Wl,--export-dynamic`, but slibtool
(which aerynOS uses) treats `-dlopen` as `-dlpreopen` and does not add
that flag, so the plugins fail to load with "undefined symbol: MSG".

Link the modules with -Wl,--export-dynamic explicitly.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
---
 src/modules/Makefile.am | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/modules/Makefile.am b/src/modules/Makefile.am
index c0f916b..a1b2c3d 100644
--- a/src/modules/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/modules/Makefile.am
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 CLEANFILES = dummy-message.wav
 
 inc_local = -I$(top_srcdir)/include -I$(top_srcdir)/src/common
+AM_LDFLAGS = -Wl,--export-dynamic
 LDFLAGS =
 
 if DARWIN_HOST
